Error [E-APP-TARGET-CAPABILITY]: App capability `.csr` needs target `JS`, but the resolved target is `Wasm`.
  --> tests/ui/app_capability_target.jet:4:29
    |
  4 | fn run() => App = web.app().csr()
    |                             ^^^
 Why: App is one type across targets, but each capability must be supported by the target selected by `#Target` or the package manifest; rejecting it in sema keeps AOT, JIT, interpreter, and web codegen on one meaning (I9).
 Fix: Choose a build target that supports `.csr` (for example `#Target(JS)` for browser capabilities or a native target for server capabilities), or remove that capability.
